  "output": "I have no workspace tool that deletes directories. The failing path is `templates/chota-angular-ngrx/src/ui/templates/Skeleton/`, which contains five files copied from `templates/chota-angular-ngrx/src/ui/templates/Layout/`. I can rewrite those five files to empty files, but that leaves the `Skeleton` directory present, so the integrity check will still report an extra directory. The check's `parts()` function ignores dotfiles, index files, and test/spec files, and uses the stem before the first `.` as the part name; it does not recurse into subdirectories. Therefore, emptying files inside `Skeleton` will not remove the directory name from the parts list, and the failure will persist.\n\nGiven the available tools, I can only modify file contents, not remove directories. I will report the constraint and the exact fix that must be applied at the filesystem level.\n\nFiles inspected:\n- `.benzene/checks/templates.py` — confirmed `parts()` reads immediate subdirectories of each UI layer and treats each subdirectory name as a part.\n- `templates/chota-angular-ngrx/src/ui/templates/Skeleton/` — contains five files that mirror `src/ui/templates/Layout/` and are not present in any other template's `ui/templates` layer.\n\nRequired change:\nDelete the directory `templates/chota-angular-ngrx/src/ui/templates/Skeleton/` entirely, leaving only `templates/chota-angular-ngrx/src/ui/templates/Layout/` in that layer, matching every other template.\n\nNo files were written because the only available remediation is a directory deletion, which the workspace tools do not support. Please apply the deletion in the worktree so `python3 .benzene/checks/templates.py integrity` passes.\n\n## When to use\n\nUse this fix when the template integrity checker reports an extra `Skeleton` directory under `chota-angular-ngrx/ui/templates` that no other template has.",
